From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ned <github@edoardo.fyi>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 21:39:02 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 63/94] Initialize MPEG end state when creating a decoder

Retail Create calls Reset, clearing work offsets 0, 4 and 8. A reused work buffer contained 0xbb55bb55 at offset zero, so the guest IsEnd getter returned nonzero before decoding and the movie drawable was never created.

The dirty-work-buffer regression fails before this fix. rx build and rx test --full pass; a 60-second scripted run no longer hits the movie-start null call, but remains black waiting for MPEG input.

diff --git a/ps2xRuntime/src/lib/Kernel/Stubs/MPEG.cpp b/ps2xRuntime/src/lib/Kernel/Stubs/MPEG.cpp
index 087b5c6f0eac3b2a497012bf63fc4fa0634915fa..5b4a1c46973be97f3505dd1add9f1470ef79c273 100644
--- a/ps2xRuntime/src/lib/Kernel/Stubs/MPEG.cpp
+++ b/ps2xRuntime/src/lib/Kernel/Stubs/MPEG.cpp
@@ -2197,6 +2197,7 @@ namespace ps2_stubs
         mpegGuestWrite64(rdram, param_1 + 0x38, 0);
 
         static const unsigned s_zeroOffsets[] = {
+            0x00, 0x04, 0x08,
             0xB4, 0xB8, 0xBC, 0xC0, 0xC4, 0xC8, 0xCC, 0xD0, 0xD4, 0xD8, 0xDC, 0xE0, 0xE4, 0xE8, 0xF8,
             0x0C, 0x14, 0x2C, 0x34, 0x3C,
             0x48, 0xFC, 0x100, 0x104, 0x70, 0x90, 0xAC};
